WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:05.220
This Italian company makes exact
reproductions of the renowned Winchesters

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.650
produced in the United States starting in
1866.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:14.760
These lever actions were a game changer in
that era because they did away with having to

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:21.630
reload your rifle one cartridge at a time to
make the barrel the long tube through which

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:26.970
the ammunition shoots the factory starts
with a bar of solid steel that's 27

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:28.530
millimetres in diameter.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.050
A computer guided circular saw slices it
into barrel length pieces.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:44.620
Next, a computer guided drill bores through
the center of each barrel length bar.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.720
The drill is fluted.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.450
This provides a channel for a continuous
high pressure flow of cutting oil, which

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:57.310
breaks down the metal shavings as the drill
advances from one end of the bar to the

00:00:57.310 --> 00:01:04.750
other. Over the course of 5 minutes, a
reamer gradually widens the bore to the

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.190
required diameter.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:08.410
This takes 15 minutes.

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:13.000
The diameter of the barrel is what
determines a firearms caliber.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.340
A rifle gets its name from the next
operation.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:27.720
This specialized tool rifles the barrel,
meaning it carves spiraled grooves into the

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.030
barrel, bores, smooth walls.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:34.680
This process takes twice as long as drilling
and reaming combined.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:40.860
The grooves in the barrel put a spin on the
cartridges bullet as it exits the gun like

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.690
the perfect pass of a football.

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:47.400
This spin stabilizes the bullet, rendering
it more aerodynamic.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.450
That makes the shot more accurate over a
long distance.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.020
The next machine mils the outside of the
barrel.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:02:01.470
This particular model has an octagonal
barrel, so the machine mills eight sides.

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:08.280
Another machine then makes threads on the
back end so the barrel can later screw into

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.050
the adjacent part of the rifle.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.540
A local foundry, meanwhile, forges the
rifles.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.180
Lever workers feed solid steel bars into a
small furnace.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:28.440
The furnace temperature a blazing 1200
degrees Celsius, softens the steel in a

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:29.760
matter of seconds.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.580
While the bar is still red hot.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.690
They place it in a dye and stamp it with a
press to bend it.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:50.410
Then two more pressings in a different die
to form the bent bar into the basic shape of

00:02:50.410 --> 00:03:00.270
the lever. A fourth pressing against a razor
sharp die this

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.250
time trims the perimeter.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.390
The roughly shaped lever is now ready for
machining in the rifle factory.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:22.290
They're a computer guided mill, works at it
for 8 minutes, meticulously shaving off bits

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.780
of steel until the leavers shape is
perfected.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:38.520
The mechanical section of the rifle is
called the action.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.930
Like a lever.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:42.240
It's forged out of a steel bar.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:48.300
Then over the course of an hour, machined to
specifications by 100 different computer

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:49.500
guided tools.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.670
This operation not only finalizes the
action's external shape.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:04.390
It also hollows out areas for the internal
components, namely the rifles, lever

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.940
activated loading and firing mechanism.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:14.020
But before that assembly happens, the action
takes a side trip to a metal treatment plant

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:17.020
where it undergoes a two step process.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:22.840
First 3 minutes submerged in a hot water
bath with special salts which harden the

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:28.360
steel. Then a quick dip in a second bath
containing a colouring chemical.

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:31.360
This gives the steel an antique finish.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:38.740
The action now returns to the gun factory to
rejoin the rifles, other components to

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:43.450
assemble the rifles, firing mechanism
workers first attach the trigger and the

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:47.260
hammer spring to a larger component called
the trigger guard.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:50.890
Then they connect the hammer itself with a
tight fitting pin.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:56.290
The Hammer Spring provides the resistance
needed for the hammer to hit the firing pin

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.870
hard enough to fire the cartridge after it's
cocked.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:06.460
Taking the action, they insert the bolt
containing the firing pin, then the firing

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:07.630
pin extension.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.440
This wedge piece links those two components.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:21.560
They insert the trigger guard into the
action, coaxing it into the correct position

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.330
with a few taps of a mallet.

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:26.900
They attach the lever underneath the trigger
guard.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.270
They mount a spring on each side of the
lever to put tension on it.

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:44.260
Then finally they connect the lever to the
firing mechanism with two sets of links to

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.410
Cock the Hammer and prepare to pull the
trigger to fire you.

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:50.020
Pull down the lever, then pull it back up.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:56.080
After firing you move the lever up and down
once again to eject the spent cartridge and

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.720
reload and cock for the next shot.

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:04.240
They finish assembling the action by
attaching side plates, one of which has a

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:06.190
side loading gate for inserting the
cartridges.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:12.730
The action has two threaded holes, one for
attaching the magazine tube that holds the

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:15.310
cartridges and the other for attaching the
barrel.

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:21.550
It's threaded and requires some top filing
in order to meet the very strict

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:26.650
specifications set out by the proof house,
the body responsible for ensuring that

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:32.470
firearms conform to all manufacturing
regulations to attach the barrel to the

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:38.050
action. They lock the barrel in a vise, then
screw the action onto the threaded end.

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:46.450
They use various tools and gauges to ensure
the two parts are perfectly aligned and that

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:49.210
the lever closes completely when pulled up.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:56.800
Next, they insert what's called a check
cartridge of the appropriate caliber into the

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:02.470
chamber. This checks the internal spacing to
ensure the ammunition feeds correctly and

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.730
fires safely.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:09.910
They mount a temporary stock on the other
end of the action and send the rifle to the

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:12.100
proof house for performance and safety
testing.

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:20.710
Their technicians place it in an enclosed
chamber, load ammunition and fire twice

00:07:28.450 --> 00:07:32.620
the proof hose, hand punches, markings onto
the bottom of the rifle.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:39.160
These markings, recognized by the European
Economic Community, officially certify that

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:42.220
the firearm functions properly and safely.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:52.470
The gun factory contracts a woodworking
company to produce the rifles stock.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.650
It's made from a block of walnut.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:01.680
First, workers trace a template that's in
the basic shape of the stalk.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.760
They saw along the trace line.

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:25.130
This gives them a starting form which
computer guided machines then refine a mill,

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:29.750
progressively carves the detailed profile
with a series of different tools.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:38.810
Then they mount the stock on a lathe which
rotates it against a sander to smooth the

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.940
surface and perfect the shape.

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:50.990
The stock has two holes in the back to which
they attach an end piece, the wood shop

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:56.300
stains and varnishes the finished stock and
sends it to the gun factory where workers

00:08:56.300 --> 00:08:57.740
attach it to the action.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:01.460
After that, they mount the magazine tube to
the action.

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.980
When you feed cartridges into the side
loading gate, they drop into the magazine

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:13.010
tube. Upon leaving the rifle, a carrier
pushes up one cartridge, which the bolt then

00:09:13.010 --> 00:09:16.430
pushes into the chamber, preparing the rifle
to fire.

